   "description": "Sixteen LEDs share one anode rail, VL, with each cathode on its own OUTn sink. C1, 10 µF, holds up the VL rail to ground. R1 from R-EXT to ground fixes the current every sink regulates. VDD is 3.3 V to 5 V. A pulse source at 0 to 100 kHz on OE/DM2 gates all outputs together. The voltage across a sink, VO at OUT0, sits between 0.3 V and 1.5 V.",
