 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Architecture",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Serial data fills a 16-bit shift register whose parallel outputs load 16 D-type latches, and each latch bit switches one of sixteen regulated current sinks. A thermal shutdown block acts on the output enable."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output current",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The sinks regulate between 5 mA and 100 mA (the recommended range starts at 3 mA). One resistor from R-EXT to ground sets the current of all channels; brightness is adjusted by its value. Current settles 40 ns (typ.) after an output turns on."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output voltage",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each output stands off up to 20 V, which allows several LEDs in series per channel. Accuracy is ± 1.5 % between bits and ± 5 % between devices with at least 1.3 V across the output, 20 mA to 100 mA, VDD 3.3 V to 5 V, 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply and logic levels",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The supply runs from 3.0 V to 5.5 V, so a 3.3 V microcontroller can drive the inputs directly. Input thresholds are 0.7 VDD and 0.3 VDD."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Serial interface",
   "page": 11,
   "text": "Each rising CLK edge shifts SDI into the 16-bit register, at up to 30 MHz (50 MHz absolute maximum); a bit reaches SDO on the sixteenth edge, so SDO can drive SDI of a following device. Latch and enable act on their levels and are independent of CLK. The latch is transparent to the shift register with LE/DM1 high and holds its data with LE/DM1 low. OE/DM2 high turns all outputs off; OE/DM2 low lets each output follow its latch bit, on for 1 and off for 0."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input structure",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Each logic input passes through a 1 kΩ series resistor to a CMOS stage, with a diode to GND at the pin. OE/DM2 has a 300 kΩ pull-up to VDD and LE/DM1 a 200 kΩ pull-down to GND; CLK and SDI have none. SDO is a CMOS push-pull output from the sixteenth bit, with a diode to GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal protection",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Thermal shutdown acts at 170 °C typical junction temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "ESD",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "ESD protection is 2 kV HBM and 200 V MM."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Exposed pad",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "On the TSSOP24 exposed pad version the pad connects to a copper land that is isolated or grounded; soldered to the board it brings RthJA to 37.5 °C/W."
  }
 ],
